WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.769 --> 00:00:03.430
(foreign language)

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:05.780
- [Narrator] After Ukrainian
president, Volodymyr Zelenskyy,

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:08.200
said the west sanctions
on Russia were not enough

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.920
to prevent further Russian
attacks on his country,

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.520
a powerful coalition
representing some of the world's

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:15.760
biggest democracies
announced it would block

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.563
some Russian banks from SWIFT.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.810
The move was part of a series
of severe economic penalties,

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:23.840
and it was seen as a significant step up

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:25.780
in the West's efforts to punish Russia

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:27.430
and its president, Vladimir Putin,

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:29.670
for its military assault on Ukraine.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.560
- The European union and its partners

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.240
are working to cripple Putin's ability

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.820
to finance his war machine.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:38.030
- [Narrator] So what is SWIFT?

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:39.890
And what does this move mean for Russia

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:41.243
and the rest of the world?

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.520
SWIFT, which stands for
the Society for Worldwide

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:47.610
Interbank Financial Telecommunication,

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:50.730
is a global system that
banks use to securely send

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.900
and receive transfer requests.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.600
Similar to how phone
networks facilitate calls,

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.943
SWIFT facilitates the movement of money.

00:00:59.712 --> 00:01:02.423
- The infrastructure is what
connects people together,

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:05.180
to be able to talk to each other.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:07.040
And this is the same thing for banks,

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:10.930
it's simply instead of ideas and love

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:13.360
and messages like that
you're sending on the phone,

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:14.270
you're sending money.

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:15.570
- [Narrator] SWIFT handles billions

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.590
of financial messages each year.

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:19.400
And while there are other systems designed

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.140
to circumvent SWIFT and challenge

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:22.620
the dominance of the dollar,

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.170
SWIFT is by far the most
commonly used system

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:26.360
around the world.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:29.380
It connects more than 11,000
financial institutions

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:32.490
in more than 200
countries and territories.

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:33.670
Headquartered in Belgium,

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:35.950
SWIFT is a member owned cooperative.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:38.323
Iran and North Korea are cut off from it.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:42.630
So how could SWIFT
sanctions impact Russia?

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:44.920
By cutting off some Russian
banks from the system,

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:46.720
the sanctions significantly hinder

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.500
the movement of money
into and out of Russia.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.200
And that could lead to higher inflation

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.200
and a weakening of the Russian Ruble.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.200
- It's like you're putting a noose

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.300
around the pipeline of money
into and out of Russia.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:00.700
- [Narrator] Not only do the sanctions aim

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:03.890
to cripple Moscow's ability to
finance the Russian military,

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.210
but they'll also affect every other aspect

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:08.410
of the economy, trickling all the way down

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:10.680
to the ability of
businesses and households

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.860
to move money outside of the country.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.270
- The leverage is the
leverage on the economy

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:18.440
and the markets, that
puts political pressure

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:22.000
internally on Putin to reverse course.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.850
- [Narrator] But SWIFT
is a global network,

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:26.100
and experts say the sanctions
could have an impact

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.220
on countries around the world.

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:31.530
Foreign banks have about
121 billion in assets

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.780
owed to them by Russian based entities.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.840
So cutting Russian banks off from SWIFT

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:38.010
could make it hard to collect that money,

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:40.280
and companies will
undoubtedly face problems

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:42.370
conducting trade with
Russian counterparts,

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:45.920
paying Russian staff, or
buying goods from Russia.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.100
However, the west is planning for now,

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:51.430
to keep some Russian banks
online for oil and gas exports

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:54.123
critical to the European
and global economies.

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:59.280
- The willingness for the
west, particularly Europe,

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:03.550
to accept these economic sacrifices,

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:07.110
which are not small, but
what that reflects is

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:11.772
the seriousness they take
Russia's actions as a threat

00:03:11.772 --> 00:03:15.100
to Western democracy, European democracy,

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:17.003
post-world war II sort of agreements.

